    "turn_idx": 5,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, that's right. One of my earliest memories is actually during Watergate. And I was six years old, maybe seven. And I remember in the mornings, my parents would wait for the Washington Post and go and sometimes send Mary and me down the little stairs. to the front porch to get the post, because that's how everybody was following all of the news about what was happening those days in Watergate. And so, no, I definitely have had the opportunity to see a lot firsthand both in my own career and before that, watching my mom and dad.",
