    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90410.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 44,
    "turn_text": "Well, let me leave the security piece. You said that you had no choice but to do what you did. At what point did you feel like I have no choice I have to do is because Trump had been talking about the election for months before the election. He pre-butted the election by saying if he didn't win it would be stolen. He really kind of, as you guys pointed out in your hearings, he kind of fanned the flames beforehand. And in fact, four years earlier, even in winning, he alleged that, you know, that millions of votes were fraudulent, and he empaneled a committee, and Vice President Pence, I think, headed the committee to try and find these imaginary votes. I mean, this was not new behavior on his part. At what point do you say, I'm going to speak out, and do you look back and say, I wish I had spoken out earlier on this?",
