    "turn_idx": 51,
    "turn_text": "And I mean, certainly you can look back in hindsight and say, well, you should have known sooner or you should have said something publicly sooner. I think that once, you know, certainly presidents have the right to challenge, okay, I'll can't, it's due of the right to challenge the outcome. Using the rules and the laws set up in each individual state, but you cannot make claims of massive fraud and illegality and then not produce any evidence of that in court and then ignore the rulings of the courts. So it was really sort of built after election day and then of course December 14th when the Electoral College met. And again, I think that many people, frankly, on both sides thought, okay, there'll be this next thing that happens and that will be the end. And of course, it wasn't. And so on January 6th itself, as soon as we were evacuated from the chamber, I knew that we had to impeach him. I knew that clearly what had happened here From you know, summoning the mob and knowing they were armed, you know, setting them up to the capital that's clearly an impeachable offense. And I think if you, you know, look at my statement a week or so after right before impeachment, I made that very clear.",
