    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90410.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 58,
    "turn_text": "Yeah. I mean, and I think if you, you know, I began immediately after my impeachment vote or the day of the vote, talking to constituents at home and talking, you know, doing local press events and talking about the extent to which none of us have the luxury or ability to only buy by the constitution or only buy by our oath when it's politically convenient and so it was clear to me what needed to be done and what i was compelled and obligated to do absolutely i had Many, many people saying to me, you know, at different periods of time, keep your head down. Don't do this. It's just better. He'll go away. This is just dividing the party and creating a real political mess. And you really shouldn't go down this path and it was inconceivable to me that that was the decision people would make.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
