    "turn_text": "I suppose this is why I think that we can't We can't look at the moment that we're into any kind of a traditional political lens. And I don't mean that with respect to me. But I also think that there's a tremendous need for people to just sort of, there's a desire for among voters, for political leaders who will just sort of say, stop, stop. the toxicity and the vitriol. But also, I think the most important thing that I can do is help to make sure that I obviously finish the job we have on the January 6th Committee and do everything I can to help people to understand and recognize how dangerous this threat is. That doesn't change depending upon poll numbers. You know, it's, it's the truth and it, you know, it's, it's, it's what I think is the most important thing for the country. And I'm sure that the members of the committee that I'm surprised to be spending time with and the Democrats that I'm surprised to be spending time with the, or surprised to be spending time with me as well. So maybe we can all learn something about what's really important here from, from each other.",
