  {
    "episode_id": 90410,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90410.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 140,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, we proceeded in a way that was very responsible, in my view, in terms of doing an investigation, gathering evidence, doing the interviews and receiving the document production, you know, close to a thousand individuals. I think it was absolutely the right sequence to say, we're going to gather all of this information. We're going to talk to all of the people that we can talk to. Of course, a number of people close to the president, the foreign president took the fifth. But that's the way investigations proceed is to gather as much information as you can before you talk to the person at the center of the effort to overturn the election. And that's how we've proceeded. Look, we are very clear-eyed about the fact that, you know, our work has to be done by the end of the year, and we've not let that, though, sort of affect the sequence in which we thought it was most responsible to do things.",
